    answer: 'When a Muslim dies, the community owes them three things: washing, shrouding with a funeral prayer, and burial, done without delay.\n\nWashing: the body is washed with water, in an odd number of washes (three, five or more), starting with the right side and the parts of wudu, and camphor goes in the last wash (Sahih al-Bukhari 1253). Men wash men and women wash women; a husband and wife may wash each other according to the schools.\n\nShrouding: the Prophet himself was wrapped in three plain white cotton sheets, with no shirt and no turban (Sahih al-Bukhari 1264). Then the funeral prayer is prayed.\n\nBurial: the Prophet said to hurry with the funeral (Sahih al-Bukhari 1315). The body is laid in the grave on its right side facing the qibla.\n\nFor the details of washing, shrouding and burying, the Huda guides in this app go step by step. Where your school differs, ask your imam.\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1253, 1264, 1315.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-janazah-wash]\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-janazah-burial]',
