    answer: 'Jumu\'ah (the Friday prayer) is two rak\'ahs, prayed in congregation at the time of Dhuhr, in place of Dhuhr. Before it, the imam gives two short sermons (khutbahs), and listening to them is part of the prayer.\n\nWho must attend: every free adult Muslim man who is a resident (not travelling) and is able to go. When the call is made on Friday, the Qur\'an says: "then proceed to the remembrance of Allah and leave trade" (Qur\'an 62:9). Women, travellers, the sick and children are not required to attend, but a woman may go if she wishes, and if she prays at home she prays Dhuhr (four rak\'ahs).\n\nSunnah acts of the day: ghusl, clean clothes, perfume (for men), going early, reciting Surah al-Kahf, and sending more blessings on the Prophet ﷺ.\n\nIf you miss Jumu\'ah, pray Dhuhr. Neglecting it is serious: the Prophet ﷺ said people must stop neglecting the Friday prayer or Allah will seal their hearts (Sahih Muslim 865).\n\nSource: Qur\'an 62:9; Sahih Muslim 865.\n[GO:/huda/guide?id=huda-jumuah]',
