      r'\bwhat is (?:a )?mahram\b',
      r'\bwho is (?:a )?mahram\b',
      r'\bmahram\b',
    ],
    answer: 'A mahram is a man a woman can never marry because of blood, marriage or nursing (such as her father, brother, son, uncle, or her husband). The Prophet ﷺ said that a woman should not travel except with a mahram (Sahih al-Bukhari 1862) (Sahih Muslim 1341).\n\nOn Hajj and Umrah, the schools differ:\n- The Hanafi and Hanbali schools make the mahram a condition: a woman without one is not required to go on Hajj, and should not go.\n- The Shafi\'i and Maliki schools allow a woman to go in a safe group of trustworthy women when the road is safe, as a condition of ability.\n- Today many scholars and authorities allow a woman to join an organised, safe pilgrimage group, relying on the safety of modern travel, while others still require the mahram. The authorities in charge of the pilgrimage also set their own entry rules, so check them before you book.\n\nThis is a real question with different opinions, so a woman in this position should ask a scholar she trusts. The Hajj is for those who are able ("to Allah from the people is a pilgrimage to the House - for whoever is able to find thereto a way" (Qur\'an 3:97)).\n\nSource: Sahih al-Bukhari 1862; Sahih Muslim 1341; Qur\'an 3:97.\n[GO:/academy/hajj-umrah-pack]',
