    avoid: <String>[
      r'\b(?:near me|nearby|app|find)\b',
    ],
    answer: 'Meat is halal when the animal is a permitted kind (cattle, sheep, goat, camel, chicken, deer, etc. - not pig, carnivores, or dead animals), and it is slaughtered properly: by a Muslim (or one of the People of the Book), with a sharp knife cutting the throat, saying "Bismillah, Allahu akbar" at the time, so that the blood flows. The Qur\'an forbids Qur\'an 5:3 dead animals, blood, pork and what is dedicated to other than Allah.\n\nWhat about meat from non-Muslims? The Qur\'an says "the food of those who were given the Scripture is lawful for you" (Qur\'an 5:5). The majority of scholars take this to mean the meat of Jews and Christians who slaughter in their religion\'s way is allowed. But many say today\'s industrial slaughter, which may not follow that, is not covered. So:\n- Safest: buy meat that is certified halal.\n- Kosher meat is accepted by many scholars as it follows a similar slaughter, though some require "Bismillah".\n- Supermarket or restaurant meat of unknown slaughter: scholars differ. Some allow it based on the verse above, citing the general rule that food is lawful unless known to be unlawful. Others say it is not allowed unless known to be halal. Following the stricter view is the common practice.\n- Stunning: allowed by many scholars if the animal is alive at the cut and would survive the stun; others reject it. Machine slaughter with a recorded "Bismillah" is also debated.\n- Fish and seafood do not need slaughter.\n\nIf you find yourself eating non-halal meat by mistake or when no halal exists, there is no sin on the one who does not know. Fast food chains differ by country and branch: check the certificate. The Masajid and Halal screen can help you find halal places.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 5:3, 5:5.\n[GO:/masajid]',
    topic: 'halal meat',
    beforeGate: true,
    reviewNote: 'Rulings on People of the Book meat, supermarket meat, stunning and machine slaughter are contested and described as differences; flagged for scholar review.',
  ),
