    answer: 'Marriage in Islam is a partnership with rights on both sides. Allah says "And due to the wives is similar to what is expected of them, according to what is reasonable" (Qur\'an 2:228), and calls the couple a source of "affection and mercy" (Qur\'an 30:21).\n\nFor the husband: to provide for his family, to treat his wife well and live with her in kindness (Qur\'an 4:19). The Prophet ﷺ said: Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1162, hasan sahih per al-Albani. And: Sunan Ibn Majah 1977, hasan per Darussalam.\n\nFor the wife: to keep the trust of the marriage, to protect the home and herself in his absence, and, as the scholars explain, to cooperate with her husband in what is right (Qur\'an 4:34 describes righteous women as "devoutly obedient, guarding in [the husband\'s] absence what Allah would have them guard" (Qur\'an 4:34)). Both should be honest and loyal to each other.\n\nIf you disagree, speak calmly, forgive the small things (Qur\'an 4:19 says perhaps you dislike a thing and Allah makes therein much good), and ask family or a counsellor to help you, as in Qur\'an 4:35. The Prophet ﷺ said: Sahih Muslim 1468.\n\nSource: Qur\'an 2:228, 30:21, 4:19, 4:34, 4:35; Jami\' at-Tirmidhi 1162, hasan sahih per al-Albani; Sunan Ibn Majah 1977, hasan per Darussalam; Sahih Muslim 1468.',
